# VibeX push policy — maps a remote-URL substring to the git user.email allowed to
# push there. The guard-bash.sh hook blocks any `git push` where the current
# user.email does not match the entry for the target remote, or where the remote is
# not listed at all.
#
# To enable: copy this file to "push-policy.conf" in the same directory and edit it
# with your real remotes and emails. push-policy.conf is gitignored, so your
# addresses stay off the repo. With no push-policy.conf present, the gate is off.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated, first matching line wins):
#   <url-substring>   <allowed-email>
#
# Examples:
#   github.com:personal   you@personal.example
#   github.com/your-user  you@personal.example
#   github.com:work       you@company.example
#   gitlab.com/acme       you@company.example
